                      (    forth6809.asm):07102         ; TSTJIDX - unit test for J. Compiles a doubly-nested DO loop:
                      (    forth6809.asm):07103         ; "DO 2 0 DO J 10 * I + + LOOP LOOP" - outer index 0..2, inner
                      (    forth6809.asm):07104         ; 0..1, accumulating (outer*10+inner) each pass. Verifies BOTH
                      (    forth6809.asm):07105         ; I and J are read correctly, and specifically at the right
                      (    forth6809.asm):07106         ; return-stack offset once genuinely nested (J's own "8,S" -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07107         ; not the "10,S" an earlier, already-documented bug used, per
                      (    forth6809.asm):07108         ; this word's own extensive bug-fix history in the source
                      (    forth6809.asm):07109         ; itself, retraced by hand here rather than assumed still
                      (    forth6809.asm):07110         ; correct). Six (outer,inner) pairs, expected sum 63 - a wrong
                      (    forth6809.asm):07111         ; nesting depth or wrong index read would produce a different
                      (    forth6809.asm):07112         ; sum, not just "some accumulation happened."
                      (    forth6809.asm):07113         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
