                      (    forth6809.asm):10227         ; TSTPOSTPONE1 - unit test for POSTPONE, normal (non-immediate)
                      (    forth6809.asm):10228         ; word case. Traced its own code first: for a normal word,
                      (    forth6809.asm):10229         ; POSTPONE compiles "[LIT xt][JSR COMPILE,]" into the current
                      (    forth6809.asm):10230         ; definition - NOT a direct call to the word itself. This is
                      (    forth6809.asm):10231         ; standard ANS semantics (POSTPONE appends a word's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):10232         ; compilation semantics to the current definition; for an
                      (    forth6809.asm):10233         ; ordinary word, that semantics IS "compile a call to it", so
                      (    forth6809.asm):10234         ; the current definition, when it later runs, must itself
                      (    forth6809.asm):10235         ; perform that compiling action against whatever definition is
                      (    forth6809.asm):10236         ; being compiled at that later point - not immediately). Given
                      (    forth6809.asm):10237         ; the genuine complexity of fully executing that second level
                      (    forth6809.asm):10238         ; (which would need a further redirected CODEHERE and a further
                      (    forth6809.asm):10239         ; round of execute-and-verify), this test instead verifies the
                      (    forth6809.asm):10240         ; compiled byte sequence directly - still a meaningful,
                      (    forth6809.asm):10241         ; unambiguous check of POSTPONE's own documented mechanism.
                      (    forth6809.asm):10242         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
