                      (    forth6809.asm):12108         ; Strings & Parsing test harness (glossary section 3.12). Reuses
                      (    forth6809.asm):12109         ; the redirect infrastructure from sections 3.8-3.10 for the
                      (    forth6809.asm):12110         ; name-parsing words (WORD/CHAR/[CHAR]/S"/."). DOTQUOTE's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):12111         ; runtime (DOTSTR) calls TYPE internally, which - per section
                      (    forth6809.asm):12112         ; 3.1's own already-debugged finding - has two entirely
                      (    forth6809.asm):12113         ; different implementations gated by SERIALPOLL; its own test
                      (    forth6809.asm):12114         ; below applies that same lesson from the start rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):12115         ; re-discovering it.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12116         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12117         ; SUBSTITUTE/REPLACES/UNESCAPE all have extensive prior-session
                      (    forth6809.asm):12118         ; bug-fix history baked into their own comments (SUBSTITUTE's
                      (    forth6809.asm):12119         ; %-delimiter algorithm, UNESCAPE's doubling-not-escaping
                      (    forth6809.asm):12120         ; behavior) - trusted as ground truth here (each confirmed via a
                      (    forth6809.asm):12121         ; prior MAME-tested session), verified fresh against the actual
                      (    forth6809.asm):12122         ; code rather than re-derived from scratch, and tested against
                      (    forth6809.asm):12123         ; that confirmed, current behavior.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12124         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):12125         
                      (    forth6809.asm):12126         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):12127         ; TSTCOUNT - unit test for COUNT. Builds a counted string at
                      (    forth6809.asm):12128         ; scratch, verifies the returned (addr len) correctly skips the
                      (    forth6809.asm):12129         ; count byte and reports its value.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12130         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
