                      (    forth6809.asm):15397         ; SECTION 27: FORTH DICTIONARY (ROM base dictionary headers)
                      (    forth6809.asm):15398         ; Every primitive word in the Glossary gets a real header here,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15399         ; chained via LINK, living in BASEDICT ($D83F-$E006, an exact fit
                      (    forth6809.asm):15400         ; for this dictionary's 1992 bytes - was $E000-$E7FF). CFA points
                      (    forth6809.asm):15401         ; directly at each primitive's own code label for every entry -
                      (    forth6809.asm):15402         ; these are all raw code entries, CFA = the label itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15403         ; including TRUE and FALSE (added in a later pass, chain's newest
                      (    forth6809.asm):15404         ; entries before H_ABORT/H_QUIT below), which originally used the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15405         ; DODOES-trampoline pattern matching interactive CONSTANT, but are
                      (    forth6809.asm):15406         ; now simple LDD/PSHU/RTS subroutines like everything else here -
                      (    forth6809.asm):15407         ; see TRUEBODY/FALSEBODY, section 26, for the current code and why
                      (    forth6809.asm):15408         ; they no longer need indirection.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15409         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):15410         ; DOES> is included (H_DOESGT) - added in a follow-up pass after
                      (    forth6809.asm):15411         ; the original 214-entry generation flagged it as missing, then
                      (    forth6809.asm):15412         ; moved again so it sits immediately after CREATE in the chain
                      (    forth6809.asm):15413         ; (H_CREATE -> H_DOESGT -> H_VARIABLE) rather than at the chain's
                      (    forth6809.asm):15414         ; newest end, since the two words are tightly coupled and read
                      (    forth6809.asm):15415         ; better adjacent. SETDOES (the runtime it compiles a call to)
                      (    forth6809.asm):15416         ; lives beside DODOES/DOESRT0; DOESGT is DOES>'s code label,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15417         ; since a literal ">" is not valid in a 6809 assembler label.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15418         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):15419         ; H_ABORT and H_QUIT (formerly ABORTHDR/QUITHDR, renamed to match
