F49D FD0100           (    forth6809.asm):20088                  STD   MVCNT      ; LDA ,X+ (needed for the byte itself)
                      (    forth6809.asm):20089                                   ; clobbers A, D's high byte, corrupting the
                      (    forth6809.asm):20090                                   ; count before SUBD used it. Unlike FILL,
                      (    forth6809.asm):20091                                   ; there's no spare 16-bit register to keep
                      (    forth6809.asm):20092                                   ; the count in instead - X and Y are both
                      (    forth6809.asm):20093                                   ; already committed to the source and
                      (    forth6809.asm):20094                                   ; destination addresses - so the fix here is
                      (    forth6809.asm):20095                                   ; reordering: decrement and store while D
