                      (    forth6809.asm):21325         ; ENVIRONMENT? - dispatcher complete; table has entries derived
                      (    forth6809.asm):21326         ; without fabricating unfixed capacities. /HOLD and /PAD were both
                      (    forth6809.asm):21327         ; added this session, answering HOLDMINSIZE and PADMINSIZE
                      (    forth6809.asm):21328         ; respectively (see each entry itself, below, for why each uses its
                      (    forth6809.asm):21329         ; own, conceptually correct constant rather than the numerically-
                      (    forth6809.asm):21330         ; equal PADOFFSET).
                      (    forth6809.asm):21331         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):21332         ; WORDLISTS (16.3.2, Search-Order word set) is deliberately absent
                      (    forth6809.asm):21333         ; from ENVTABLE, not an oversight - this system doesn't implement
                      (    forth6809.asm):21334         ; the Search-Order word set, so WORDLISTS is genuinely an unknown
                      (    forth6809.asm):21335         ; attribute here. Per ENVIRONMENT?'s own spec (6.1.1345): "If the
                      (    forth6809.asm):21336         ; system treats the attribute as unknown, the returned flag is
                      (    forth6809.asm):21337         ; false" - falling through to ENVNOTFOUND already produces exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):21338         ; that, correctly and completely, with no dispatcher work needed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):21339         ; Confirmed via MAME testing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):21340         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):21341         ; MAX-D/MAX-UD were resolved this session via a genuine dispatcher
                      (    forth6809.asm):21342         ; extension, not just a table entry - both are double-cell values
                      (    forth6809.asm):21343         ; per their own ANS data type, which the original single-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):21344         ; ENVFOUND (pushing exactly one value before TRUE) couldn't
                      (    forth6809.asm):21345         ; represent. Added a second table (ENVTABLE2) and matching loop
                      (    forth6809.asm):21346         ; (ENV2START/ENV2LOOP/ENV2FOUND, below) specifically for double-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):21347         ; entries, rather than reworking the single-cell path to handle both
                      (    forth6809.asm):21348         ; shapes - see those labels for the full design.
                      (    forth6809.asm):21349         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):21350         ; FLOORED was the third, separate open item flagged previously -
                      (    forth6809.asm):21351         ; investigated this session by tracing DIVCOMMON (shared by /, MOD,
                      (    forth6809.asm):21352         ; /MOD) against this system's own SM/REM and FM/MOD. Confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):21353         ; DIVCOMMON matches SM/REM's convention exactly (remainder sign
